# .env.example — a template. Copy it, fill it in, and source it YOURSELF.
#
# Nothing in this repository reads a .env file. There is no dotenv dependency and no
# loader, and that is deliberate rather than unfinished: a tool that silently absorbs
# whatever happens to sit in a file on disk cannot tell you which key it used, and
# `provenance.provider` would stop being an answer to "what produced this run?".
#
# So this file signals that the variables below are the ones that matter. It does not
# make them take effect.
#
#   PowerShell   $env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY = 'YOUR_KEY_HERE'      (this session only)
#   bash / zsh   export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY='YOUR_KEY_HERE'
#
# Replace the words YOUR_KEY_HERE. Do not paste a line as written — a value containing
# angle brackets, quotes or whitespace is refused before dispatch, because that shape
# is a placeholder rather than a key. See `implausibleKeyReason` in scripts/run-eval.ts.
#
# Copy this to `.env` if you like keeping it on disk; `.env` is gitignored, this file
# is the one deliberate exception.

# Enables `npm run eval -- --live` and the live provider path. Absent, every run
# degrades to a labelled demo placeholder and says so — that is the honesty guarantee
# working, not a failure.
#
# A live run sends prompts to api.anthropic.com and spends money. It additionally
# requires an explicit --max-calls budget; there is no default.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=''
